body:
When the FanDuel golf event name doesn't match the ESPN event name, the `event_group` will be created but the `event` will not, and we wind up with errors.

```
The bug is on line 131-140 of syncGolfEvents():

if (!existingEvent) {
  const eventGroup = await this.createEventGroup({
    name: fanduelEvent.name,
    sportLeague: 'GOLF',
  });

  const espnMatch = espnSchedule.find((espn) =>
    this.normalizeEventName(espn.name).includes(this.normalizeEventName(fanduelEvent.name)),
  );
  if (espnMatch){
    await this.createEvent({
      eventGroupId: eventGroup.eventGroupId,
      name: fanduelEvent.name,
      startDate: espnMatch?.startDate,
      endDate: espnMatch?.endDate,
      externalEventId: fanduelEvent.id,
      externalEventSource: 'FANDUEL',
    });
  }
}

The event group is created first (line 123-126), then the code tries to find a matching ESPN event to create the actual event row. If no matching ESPN event is found (espnMatch is undefined), the if (espnMatch) guard on line 131 skips the createEvent call entirely.

So the scenario is:
1. FanDuel returns a golf event that doesn't have a corresponding match in the ESPN PGA schedule
2. The event group is created (no dedup check since externalEventId wasn't found)
3. No event row is created because espnMatch is falsy
4. The result: an orphaned EVENT_GROUP with no EVENT rows

This happens when the FanDuel golf tournament name doesn't match any ESPN schedule event name after normalization. Name mismatches between the two data sources could be caused by:
- Different naming conventions ("The Masters" vs "Masters Tournament")
- Different capitalization or punctuation
- FanDuel listing a tournament that ESPN doesn't cover in their schedule responseFound it. In syncGolfEvents() at events.service.ts:131-140:

const eventGroup = await this.createEventGroup({ name: fanduelEvent.name, sportLeague: 'GOLF' });

const espnMatch = espnSchedule.find(/* name match */);
if (espnMatch) {                                  // <--- gate
  await this.createEvent({ ... });                // only called when match found
}

The event group is created first, unconditionally (line 123). Then the code tries to find a matching ESPN schedule entry for date info. If espnMatch is null (name mismatch between FanDuel and ESPN), the createEvent is skipped entirely — leaving an orphaned EVENT_GROUP with zero EVENT rows.

This would happen whenever a FanDuel golf tournament name doesn't normalize-match to any ESPN PGA schedule entry (e.g., naming differences, special characters, or tournament not in the ESPN schedule). Each call to findEventGroupsBySportLeague('GOLF') re-runs the sync, so it would keep trying to create the same group on every request — but since findEventByExternalEvent only checks events (not groups), it sees no existing event and creates another orphaned group.

Fix: Move the createEventGroup inside the if (espnMatch) guard, so the group is only created when you know you can also create the event:

if (espnMatch) {
  const eventGroup = await this.createEventGroup({ ... });
  await this.createEvent({ ... });
}
```
